 "honest": [
  "at BOOK level (b) and (c) are the same computation, so 'the book offset is compounding' is an identity, not a finding; the finding is what is left at ENGINE level once that identity is subtracted",
  "a book whose daily walk and month walk disagree is reported in book_level_mismatches instead of being netted into the engine residual -- a calendar edge must not look like a cross term",
  "(c) is rebuilt from the same curves the published arm face reads, so published_level_rebuilt_from_days is a wiring check, not a second opinion on the level",
  "this leg changes no published level: it says whether the decomposition may be quoted for levels, and at what tolerance"
 ],
